# IMPORTANT: a .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the EAS Build upload — it does
# NOT extend it. So this must repeat everything .gitignore excludes, or those
# files (node_modules, ios/Pods, .git) balloon the archive. A bare .easignore
# that listed only extras made the upload 3.2 GB and blew the 2 GB limit.
#
# ios/ + android/ are excluded on purpose: this project is CNG (they're generated
# and gitignored), so EAS runs `expo prebuild` to regenerate them from app.json +
# the config plugins + the committed GoogleService-Info.plist. Do NOT ship the
# local ios/ — its Pods dir alone is gigabytes.

# --- mirror of .gitignore ---
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env*.local
*.tsbuildinfo
example
/ios
/android
*.ipa
.gstack/

# --- EAS-only extras (not in .gitignore, and untracked so a .easignore must
#     name them explicitly or they get swept into the upload) ---
.git/
proxy/
**/*.log
# Claude worktrees/scratch — not app code, ~GBs of nested Pods.
.claude/
# The on-device Gemma weights (~2.4 GB). The niyora-gemma podspec bundles NO model
# resource — weights are downloaded into Application Support at runtime — so the
# build does not need this dir. (The vendored CLiteRTLM.xcframework IS needed and
# stays.) Dropping it is what keeps the archive under EAS's 2 GB limit.
modules/niyora-gemma/ios/model/
